From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: defcom5-rockchip <286489597+defcom5-rockchip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 15:21:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] arm64: dts: rockchip: orangepi-5: bump CMA pool 256M ->
 1024M

The board's linux,cma-default region (in rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts, which
overrides the 8MB generic node in rk3588-linux.dtsi) was fixed at 256MB
for the hdmirx controller. Raise it to 1024MB for headroom with
multi-stream 4K decode/encode and HDMI-in capture.

Switch from a fixed `reg` to a `size`-based reservation so the kernel
auto-places the larger 1GB region rather than pinning it at 0x10000000.

Note: not strictly required for the VOP2 4K@120Hz display fix (framebuffer
size is independent of refresh rate); this is extra video-memory headroom.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1cb82d029cedd3074b41dcac173e71f35583609e)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
index 71d4a6b54290..9e87a97cf288 100755
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
@@ -263,11 +263,16 @@ reserved-memory {
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
 
-		/* Reserve 256MB memory for hdmirx-controller@fdee0000 */
+		/*
+		 * CMA pool for hdmirx-controller@fdee0000, VPU and display.
+		 * Bumped 256MB -> 1024MB for headroom (multi-stream 4K
+		 * decode/encode, HDMI-in capture). Use size= so the kernel
+		 * auto-places the larger region instead of a fixed reg.
+		 */
 		cma {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			reusable;
-			reg = <0x0 (256 * 0x100000) 0x0 (256 * 0x100000)>;
+			size = <0x0 (1024 * 0x100000)>;
 			linux,cma-default;
 		};
 	};
